"""Prompt templates for the constrained Ollama planner."""

SYSTEM_PROMPT = """Create a browser test plan as JSON only. Top-level keys are exactly `name`, `steps`, `assertions`. Use ONLY these actions: navigate, click, fill, select, check, radio, wait. Every target has `by` (role, label, placeholder, text, or css) and `value`. For by=role, value is an ARIA role such as button or link; it may also have `name` set to the accessible name. For other strategies, value is the label, placeholder, exact text, or CSS selector. For a text target, use the exact text named in the instruction. navigate has `action` and `url` only. click and wait have `action` and `target` only. fill has `action`, `target`, `value` (text to enter). select has `action`, `target`, `option`. check is ONLY for checking a checkbox; radio is ONLY for selecting a radio input. These actions must target an input or its associated label. Do NOT use `check` to mean verify, confirm, or assert. All requested checks of page title, visible text, URL, or element visibility MUST be represented as `assertions`, never as action steps. Assertions use `kind` (title, text, url, visible) and `expected`; visible also needs a target object. For a URL assertion, `expected` must be only the literal URL substring requested (for example `/demo`), without words such as “contains” or “URL”. For a simple page-load check, use exactly one navigate action and make the requested URL or title check an assertion; do not add a redundant wait, click, or text locator. Do not include irrelevant keys. Never invent credentials or selectors. Use only information in the instruction and public page context. Never submit payments, delete data, or bypass authentication."""


def user_prompt(instruction: str, base_url: str) -> str:
    return f"Base URL: {base_url}\nInstruction: {instruction}\nReturn the JSON test plan now."
